# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but the documented template is meant to be committed.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Video masters now live in assets/video-masters/, outside public/, so they are
# retained without being served — the same convention assets/creative-masters/
# and assets/editorial-masters/ already follow. The web derivatives in
# public/videos/ are what ship.
#
# testimonial-bg.mp4 stays ignored on top of that: it is 111 MiB, over GitHub's
# 100 MiB hard limit, so committing it makes the branch unpushable. Keep it in
# shared storage (or Git LFS) rather than in history.
/assets/video-masters/testimonial-bg.mp4

# Payload runtime files. Both live on the host's persistent disk next to the
# checkout and are backed up with the database — never committed
# (docs/cms/SPEC.md §A.3). `media/` is the Media collection's upload dir;
# `private/` holds generated invoice PDFs and anything else that must not be
# served from public/.
/media/
/private/
